HAI 1.2
  BTW  Functions defined here are spliced ahead of every test, because LOLCODE
  BTW  has no import. Keep the HAI and KTHXBYE: the runner strips them.
  BTW
  BTW  BTW is a comment to the end of the line and OBTW ... TLDR is the block
  BTW  form. Both have to start a statement -- LOLCODE is one statement per
  BTW  line, so a comment cannot follow code on the same line.
  BTW
  BTW  A comment outside the HAI and KTHXBYE would be lost, because the runner
  BTW  strips those markers and splices only what is between them.
  BTW
  BTW  HOW IZ I declares a function and YR introduces a parameter. IF U SAY SO
  BTW  closes it. A second parameter would be AN YR, and that is the whole of
  BTW  the signature -- there are no types to declare.
  HOW IZ I greet YR who
    BTW  FOUND YR is the return. A function is the only place a branch can
    BTW  produce a value in this language, because O RLY? and WTF? are
    BTW  statements rather than expressions -- so FOUND YR is the way out of
    BTW  each arm of one.
    BTW
    BTW  SMOOSH concatenates and AN separates its operands, with MKAY closing
    BTW  the call. It is the whole string library: there is no length, no
    BTW  substring and no split, which is why the course here starts with
    BTW  Leap years rather than FizzBuzz.
    FOUND YR SMOOSH "Hello, " AN who AN "!" MKAY
  IF U SAY SO
KTHXBYE
